[20:46:01] 💭 Now I understand the unparam logic precisely:

```go
reason := "is unused"
constStr := c.alwaysReceivedConst(callSites, par, i)
if constStr != "" {
    reason = fmt.Sprintf("always receives %s", constStr)
} else if c.anyRealUse(par, i, pkg) {
    c.debug("  skip - used somewhere in the func body\n")
    continue
}
c.addIssue(fn, par.Pos(), "%s %s", par.Name(), reason)
```

So the logic is:
1. If the param "always receives the same constant" (from callers) → report "always receives X".
2. Else if…
[20:46:02] The unparam logic is clear: params not used in the body with <4 call sites are reported "is unused". Let me check how golangci-lint invokes unparam to confirm.


